# Node.js Web Server

## About
I made this project to learn how a web server works in Node.js.
In this project, I used the HTTP module to create a server. The server checks which page the user wants and sends that page to the browser. If the page is not found, it shows a 404 page.

## What I Used
Node.js
JavaScript
HTML
CSS

## Project Files
server.js
pages folder
public folder
README.md
package.json

## Pages in the Project
Home Page
About Page
Services Page
Contact Page
404 Error Page

## How to Run the Project
Open the project in VS Code.
Open the terminal.
Run this command.
```bash
node server.js
```
Now open your browser and go to
```
http://localhost:3000
```
You can also open
```
http://localhost:3000/home
http://localhost:3000/about
http://localhost:3000/services
http://localhost:3000/contact
```
## How the Server Works
When a user opens the website, the browser sends a request to the server.
The server checks the URL.
If the page is available, it reads the HTML file and sends it to the browser.
If the page is not available, it sends the 404 page.
The server also sends the CSS file so that the pages look properly designed.

## What I Learned
While making this project I learned how to create a web server.
I learned how routing works.
I learned the difference between request and response.
I learned how to read HTML files using `fs.readFile()`.
I also learned how to send CSS files and how to create a custom 404 page.

## Problems I Faced
At first I found it difficult to understand routing.
I also had some confusion while serving the CSS file.
After practicing and testing different routes, I understood how the server works.

## Future Improvements
In the future I want to make this project using Express.js.
I also want to connect it with a database.
I would like to add forms and make the website more interactive.